                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "84add4cf-7620-3bb3-bd40-c897ae60e2d3",
                        "entry_id": "c14ea6b2-7ce9-3b9f-9009-4f39160ab5d7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "verschijnsel dat binnen de poolcirkels de zon boven de horizon zichtbaar blijft voor een periode van minstens 24 uur (op de poolcirkel) tot hoogstens een halfjaar (op de Noord- of Zuidpool)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c45b57b-89a6-4156-a2a7-094a0cb6482a",
                                "sense_id": "84add4cf-7620-3bb3-bd40-c897ae60e2d3",
                                "text": "De middernachtzon duurt in Lapland van begin juni tot halverwege juli. Op Spitsbergen begint de middernachtzon al in april en eindigt 'ie eind augustus."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4aa5bae2-faee-3fa8-b5f4-05904241a00e",
                        "entry_id": "c14ea6b2-7ce9-3b9f-9009-4f39160ab5d7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "zon, zoals die binnen de poolcirkels minstens een periode van 24 uur zichtbaar blijft boven de horizon"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a281fb80-0a13-408d-94a4-dda9213a7f86",
                                "sense_id": "4aa5bae2-faee-3fa8-b5f4-05904241a00e",
                                "text": "De middernachtzon schijnt."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4faa5726-be04-403e-b467-59d80c711bc4",
                                "sense_id": "4aa5bae2-faee-3fa8-b5f4-05904241a00e",
                                "text": "Onder een dubbele regenboog, met de middernachtzon in mijn achteruitkijkspiegel, rijd ik naar Skoganvarre."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "abe01734-86ee-4c83-bdb0-7f022bdb9a21",
                        "source_entry_id": "c14ea6b2-7ce9-3b9f-9009-4f39160ab5d7",
                        "target_lang_word": "Mitternachtssonne",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d43e3387-e52d-402f-ab70-fa4ccefbe3d9",
                        "source_entry_id": "c14ea6b2-7ce9-3b9f-9009-4f39160ab5d7",
                        "target_lang_word": "midnight sun",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "midnight sun",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7a1dd917-5e99-33f1-b22b-dd3acde4195b",
                                        "entry_id": "636a1229-f279-3552-81b6-6570924bafdb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The phenomenon occurring when the Sun does not set but only approaches the horizon at midnight; it occurs near the summer solstice in the polar regions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c90b0f45-3b03-4f93-ba0c-b66b4affd62a",
                                                "sense_id": "7a1dd917-5e99-33f1-b22b-dd3acde4195b",
                                                "text": "He has only retained three engravings; namely, a map of the country, which is very little known, from Torneo to North Cape; a View of Torneo by the midnight moon; and a View of North Cape by the midnight sun."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54fed81d-b5d4-4ffa-ae59-89c708eb8308",
                                                "sense_id": "7a1dd917-5e99-33f1-b22b-dd3acde4195b",
                                                "text": "Locked icebergs splintering through the awful night; / And quenchless midnight suns with their wild scarlet light."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57cf9c60-263a-4b6d-96de-e617a1993692",
                                                "sense_id": "7a1dd917-5e99-33f1-b22b-dd3acde4195b",
                                                "text": "This wonderful midnight sun has a peculiar effect on the polar vegetation. Although the foliage of ligneous plants, such as shrubs and trees, which here sink down to the condition of dwarfs, is tough and coriaceous, and of a dark and sombre green, gloomy as the long night of the polar world, yet in the steady light which comes from the sun as he circulates above the horizon for weeks, that sombre green tint of the foliage is beautifully softened in the grasses and other herbaceous plants."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66f5350a-fe69-4ba8-8519-c4341ae7107a",
                                                "sense_id": "7a1dd917-5e99-33f1-b22b-dd3acde4195b",
                                                "text": "But when we come to the winter solstice, we get no more midnight suns: as shown in the figure, all the circle is situated in the shaded portion; hence, again in spite of the Earth's rotation, we cannot get out of the darkness, and we do not see the Sun even at noonday."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f59a7e5-55e0-4350-a600-2ddd4f224edb",
                                                "sense_id": "7a1dd917-5e99-33f1-b22b-dd3acde4195b",
                                                "text": "Like the seasons, the \"Midnight Sun\" has its origin in the inclination of the earth's axis during its annual motion. […] The effect of this inclination is to produce variations in the length of the day to such an extent, that in polar regions the duration of sunlight is reckoned in months instead of hours."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d24da36-5a3d-4bad-ba22-a07e8ecf6bb3",
                                                "sense_id": "7a1dd917-5e99-33f1-b22b-dd3acde4195b",
                                                "text": "There are strange things done in the midnight sun / By the men who moil for gold; / The Arctic trails have their secret tales / That would make your blood run cold; / The Northern Lights have seen queer sights, / But the queerest they ever did see / Was that night on the marge of Lake Lebarge / I cremated Sam McGee."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e0198df5-718a-4d63-92c5-7c01748ed69c",
                        "source_entry_id": "c14ea6b2-7ce9-3b9f-9009-4f39160ab5d7",
                        "target_lang_word": "soleil de minuit",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "soleil de minuit",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1adf048d-5076-3843-8499-33fd2c5ed133",
                                        "entry_id": "8fea7786-3d04-3926-bc8a-12a3d1120947",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Soleil qui apparaît toute la journée et donc à minuit lors de certains solstices dans les cercles polaires."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "597ff022-6474-4426-ad19-bca6cda78425",
                                                "sense_id": "1adf048d-5076-3843-8499-33fd2c5ed133",
                                                "text": "Et ce soir même, ces hardis pionniers, […] , virent l’astre radieux raser les bords de l’horizon occidental, sans même y échancrer son disque flamboyant.\nLe soleil de minuit brillait pour la première fois à leurs yeux."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9db737c5-f149-4f38-8316-c7277476ebdb",
                                                "sense_id": "1adf048d-5076-3843-8499-33fd2c5ed133",
                                                "text": "[…], et en moins de temps qu’il ne faut pour le dire, soleil, côtes, mer, tout s’évanouissait dans un affreux brouillard si épais qu’on eût pu le couper en tranches. Il était alors onze heures et demie du soir. Adieu le soleil de minuit ! adieu le cap Nord ! Les Anglaises durent rengainer leurs pinceaux ; peindre le soleil de minuit était leur désir le plus cher, et voila que l’astre s’éclipsait au bon moment !"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3450c339-a688-4c01-a87a-890feac3d3df",
                                                "sense_id": "1adf048d-5076-3843-8499-33fd2c5ed133",
                                                "text": "Pour ajouter à l’inconfort, le soleil tape 24 heures par jour ces temps-ci, en raison du soleil de minuit."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
